<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cassĭtĕrum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ron</span></b> ), i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσίτερος</span>, orig.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mixture</i>
			or <i>alloy of lead</i>, <i>silver</i>,
				<i>and other metals;</i> afterwards <i>tin</i> (= plumbum album), <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				16, 47, § 156</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Avien. Or.
				Mar. 260</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 21</span></i>
			P.; <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 315</span></i> ib.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cassĭtĕrĭnus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσιτέρινος</span>, <i>made of tin</i>:
			lamella, Pelagon. Vet. 7.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
